EC2 Auto Startup Script – Setup Guide
1. Objective
This document explains how to automatically start Docker containers.

2. Prerequisites
Ubuntu EC2 instance
Docker installed and running
Docker Compose installed

3. Startup Script Location
Create script file:
/opt/start-all.sh


4. Startup Script
#!/bin/bash

LOG_FILE="/var/log/ec2-startup.log"

# Clear old log
echo "" > $LOG_FILE
echo "===== EC2 Startup Started at $(date) =====" >> $LOG_FILE


# -----------------------------------
# 1. Start Container 
# -----------------------------------
echo "Starting Container..." >> $LOG_FILE
cd /home/ubuntu/fabric-samples/test-network

./network.sh up -ca -s couchdb >> $LOG_FILE 2>&1

sleep 30


5. Give Permission
chmod +x /opt/start-all.sh


6. Create Systemd Service
File:
sudo nano /etc/systemd/system/ec2-startup.service

Content:
[Unit]
Description=EC2 Full Startup Script
After=network.target docker.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=ubuntu
ExecStart=/opt/start-all.sh
RemainAfterExit=yes
TimeoutStartSec=0

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target


7. Enable Service
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable ec2-startup.service


8. Start Service Manually (Optional)
sudo systemctl start ec2-startup.service


9. Check Status
sudo systemctl status ec2-startup.service

Expected output:
Active: active (exited)


10. Check Logs
cat /var/log/ec2-startup.log


